From 7638f5ed1dd132293b1a4de8358a91e97643deab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:39:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): serialize legacy creation-key replay checks
 [daveey]

The real CLI concurrency acceptance exposed a pre-existing legacy race: both creators could miss the early lookup, while only strict native admission rechecked inside write_txn. Recheck every keyed creation there; retain strict receipt checks and archived-key semantics. Deterministic barrier RED on 3ebbb87 returns two IDs; GREEN deduplicates tasks and created events. Distinct/no-key and archived reuse controls plus actual CLI timeout/ambiguous-response coverage remain.

Isolate receipt-artifact process inventory from unrelated host process churn while preserving deletion assertions and a real fail-closed scan-unavailable control. Original broad run had four cleanup assertion failures; isolated greens do not identify their historical cause. Controlled inventory failure reproduces all four, without any production cleanup change. Nine focused files389passed without retries; scripts/check21passed.
